<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
	Release-configuration entitlements (todo 286). Wired into the Release build
	config only, via CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS in Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj;
	Debug and Profile stay on Runner.entitlements with `development`, which keeps
	the on-device dev push loop (`flutter run`) working.

	`production` is what a Distribution-signed archive must carry — App Store
	Connect validation rejects a `development` APNs entitlement. Keep any future
	entitlement added to Runner.entitlements mirrored here.

	Still outstanding before the first TestFlight/App Store archive: the APNs
	authentication key must exist in the Apple Developer account and be uploaded
	to the Firebase console (iOS app -> Cloud Messaging -> APNs Authentication
	Key). The entitlement value only matters once it matches real provisioning.
	See docs/DEPLOYMENT_SECURITY_CHECKLIST.md -> Mobile (Flutter).
-->
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>production</string>
</dict>
</plist>
